# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA POLICY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decision taken by the authors: the raw data is tracked and published.
# Tracked accordingly:
#   tensile_samples_data.csv, selected_all_samples*.csv   experimental strengths
#   crack_digitized_data/                14 digitized laboratory traces
#   outputs/fields/ddm_crack_sample_*.csv      14 model-derived traces
#   outputs/fields/fields_npz/           14 cached field archives (36 MB) - these
#                                        make the validation tables and figures
#                                        reproducible without the multi-hour
#                                        notebook run
#   outputs/fields/smoke_*.csv           step-wise crack diagnostics
#   selected_all_samples.xls             original spreadsheet, retained as the
#                                        source format alongside its CSV export
# No data file is excluded.

# Executed notebook copies are large (33 MB) and regenerable
outputs/tables/executed_notebooks/

# Solver caches. These are keyed on a hash of the specimen geometry and
# material, so they rebuild themselves when anything they depend on changes;
# committing them would only pin a stale solve.
outputs/fields/_cache_*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Present locally, deliberately not part of the published code release
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pre-refactor notebooks that scripts/extract_analysis_sections.py reads,
# plus the two full DDM solver notebooks. Keep them: they are the source the
# generated tools/analysis/ modules come from, and the only way to rebuild the
# cached field archives from scratch. They are not published because they carry
# ~76 MB of stored output images and are superseded by the generated package.
legacy_notebooks/

# The paper itself. Publishing the manuscript alongside the software is not the
# usual practice, and nothing in the code reads from here.
manuscript/

# Historical and exploratory material, superseded by the current analysis.
archive/

# Cloud-sync scratch directories, not project content.
.tmp.driveupload/
.backup_0809/
